From 9db4b056378157fce85e0d8f73518f256013db03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:58:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Round 9: Skip the hot bracket evaluation when a floor
 proves the target

Vapor enthalpy and entropy at 1073.15 K fall with pressure, so a
process-wide table on 64 log-spaced pressures gives a floor for the hot
bracket end. A target below the floor is inside the bracket and the
exact evaluation is skipped; otherwise the previous evaluation and
comparison run, so infeasible classification is unchanged. The Newton
start uses the table interpolated in ln p when the evaluation is
skipped. A unit test scans 20,000 pressures. Values change in the last
bits.

Workload: domain (48 candidates at 950 K), matrix API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 0.129 ms -> 0.111 ms, 1.16x (paired 1.14x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.128 ms -> 0.116 ms, paired 1.12x.
validate.py passed against the release CLI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
